  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      9.1 • Comprehensive Review\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      Grand Revision — <hlt>Part 2</hlt>\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Synthesizing algorithmic logic and data structures before taking the final exam and 5 capstones!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #86efac; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #111111; padding: 16px;\">\n      <span style=\"display: inline-block; background: #fff; border: 2px solid #111; padding: 2px 6px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; margin-bottom: 6px;\">\n        1. Control Flow & Loops\n      </span>\n      <p style=\"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;\">\n        • <code>if / elif / else</code> evaluate top-down.<br/>\n        • <code>for item in list:</code> traverses sequences.<br/>\n        • <code>while condition:</code> repeats until False.\n      </p>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #c4b5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #111111; padding: 16px;\">\n      <span style=\"display: inline-block; background: #fff; border: 2px solid #111; padding: 2px 6px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; margin-bottom: 6px;\">\n        2. Functions & Data Structures\n      </span>\n      <p style=\"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;\">\n        • <code>def fn(param): return val</code> packages logic.<br/>\n        • <strong>Lists:</strong> <code>[0, 1, 2]</code>, <code>.append()</code>, <code>.pop()</code>.<br/>\n        • <strong>Dicts:</strong> <code>{\"k\": \"v\"}</code>, <code>.get(k, default)</code>.\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
